    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33887" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">părĭto</span></b> ,
		āre, v. freq. a.
		1. paro, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to prepare</i>, <i>get ready</i>, <i>be about</i> to do a thing (Plautin.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quo nunc ire paritas?</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Merc. 3, 4, 64</span></i>
			.—With <i>ut</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ecquas viginti minas Paritas ut a med auferas?</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Ps. 1, 5, 71</span></i>
			.</div>
